WEBVTT

00:09:28.596 --> 00:09:32.116
Another animal ... that we
like are prawns, right?

00:09:32.156 --> 00:09:33.636
Everyone loves to eat a prawn.

00:09:33.636 --> 00:09:36.556
That there is the last, the deepest
of the big crustaceans.

00:09:36.596 --> 00:09:39.876
That's a prawn, and those
are down to nearly 8,000 metres.

00:09:39.916 --> 00:09:43.476
And that wouldn't look
that out of place in a fish market.

00:09:43.476 --> 00:09:45.316
There's nothing weird about it either.

00:09:45.316 --> 00:09:48.556
And one of my personal favorites
from the very, very, deepest points,

00:09:48.596 --> 00:09:52.116
and we see these bizarrely at the very
deepest points in multiple trenches,

00:09:52.156 --> 00:09:55.756
we very rarely see them anywhere else
except for the most extreme places.

00:09:55.796 --> 00:09:57.876
And it's a type of anemone.

00:09:58.436 --> 00:10:02.556
And they just kind of look
like white flowers floating in the wind.